stage: decode
panic: attempt to add with overflow
site: src/decode.rs:280:28
repro: cargo fuzz run fuzz_opcode_decode fuzz/crashes/fuzz_opcode_decode/719b3a5e2b9b
input bytes: 2b 37 ff ff ff ff 25

Distinct from 2ca4d9928955 (F3rc start_reg overflow). This site is
`read_unit`: `let off = insns_off + ((pc + unit_idx) as usize) * 2;`.
u32 `pc` advances through the decode loop and can approach u32::MAX on
large synthesized `insns_size` values — then `pc + unit_idx` overflows.

Filed during dex-hardening's fuzz re-smoke (directive #7). Handed off
to `dex-hardening-sweep` for fix: `pc.checked_add(unit_idx)` and return
`DexError::TruncatedInstruction` on overflow, or clamp `insns_size` at
the parser boundary before it ever feeds `decode_insns`.
